IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2014(h) to (n): emergency standards, sponsored aliens, third-party assistance, on-the-job training, the self-employed, child support.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Seams taken as inputs, named for the answering section: s 2012(j) (the household includes an elderly or disabled member), s 2015(f)(2)(B) (the alien described there),
-- s 2017 (the maximum monthly allotment), s 2014(d)(11) (a payment or allowance described there; answered in snap1-s2014-d).

§ `s 2014(h) Emergency standards`

-- src:430 | The Secretary shall, after consultation with the official empowered to exercise the authority provided for by sections 5170a and 5192 of title 42, establish temporary emergency standards of eligibility for the duration of the emergency for households who are victims of a disaster which disrupts commercial channels of food distribution, if such households are in need of temporary food assistance and if commercial channels of food distribution have again become available to meet the temporary food needs of such households.
@ref s 2014(h)(1), first sentence (src:430)
GIVEN `the household is a victim of a disaster which disrupts commercial channels of food distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is in need of temporary food assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `commercial channels of food distribution have again become available to meet the temporary food needs of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(h)(1) the Secretary must establish temporary emergency standards of eligibility for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the household is a victim of a disaster which disrupts commercial channels of food distribution`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "households who are victims of a disaster which disrupts commercial channels of food distribution"
        IF `the household is in need of temporary food assistance` AND `commercial channels of food distribution have again become available to meet the temporary food needs of the household`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall ... establish temporary emergency standards of eligibility for the duration of the emergency for households who are victims of a disaster"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if such households are in need of temporary food assistance and if commercial channels of food distribution have again become available to meet the temporary food needs of such households" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:435 | The Secretary shall provide, by regulation, for emergency allotments to eligible households to replace food destroyed in a disaster. The regulations shall provide for replacement of the value of food actually lost up to a limit approved by the Secretary
@ref s 2014(h)(3)(A), the entitlement (src:435)
GIVEN `the household is an eligible household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household's food was destroyed in a disaster` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(h)(3)(A) the household is provided an emergency allotment to replace food destroyed in a disaster` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is an eligible household` AND `the household's food was destroyed in a disaster`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "emergency allotments to eligible households to replace food destroyed in a disaster"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the allotments are "to eligible households to replace food destroyed in a disaster"

-- src:435 | (A) The Secretary shall provide, by regulation, for emergency allotments to eligible households to replace food destroyed in a disaster. The regulations shall provide for replacement of the value of food actually lost up to a limit approved by the Secretary not greater than the applicable maximum monthly allotment for the household size.
@ref s 2014(h)(3)(A), the amount (src:435)
GIVEN `the value of the food actually lost, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit approved by the Secretary, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2017 the maximum monthly allotment for the household size, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(h)(3)(A) the value of the food replaced` MEANS
    minimum (LIST `the value of the food actually lost, in dollars`, `the limit approved by the Secretary, in dollars`, `s 2017 the maximum monthly allotment for the household size, in dollars`)

DECLARE `s 2014(h)(3)(B) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 2014(h)(3)(B) the availability of the State agency's offices and personnel`
    `s 2014(h)(3)(B) conditions that make reliance on electronic benefit transfer systems impracticable`
    `s 2014(h)(3)(B) damage to or disruption of transportation and communication facilities`

-- src:436 | In making this adjustment, the Secretary shall consider the availability of the State agency’s offices and personnel, any conditions that make reliance on electronic benefit transfer systems described in section 2016(h) of this title impracticable, and any damage to or disruption of transportation and communication facilities.
@ref s 2014(h)(3)(B), the factors (src:436)
`s 2014(h)(3)(B) the factors the Secretary must consider` MEANS
    LIST `s 2014(h)(3)(B) the availability of the State agency's offices and personnel`
       , `s 2014(h)(3)(B) conditions that make reliance on electronic benefit transfer systems impracticable`
       , `s 2014(h)(3)(B) damage to or disruption of transportation and communication facilities`

-- src:436 | (B) The Secretary shall adjust issuance methods and reporting and other application requirements to be consistent with what is practicable under actual conditions in the affected area. In making this adjustment, the Secretary shall consider the availability of the State agency’s offices and personnel, any conditions that make reliance on electronic benefit transfer systems described in section 2016(h) of this title impracticable, and any damage to or disruption of transportation and communication facilities.
@ref s 2014(h)(3)(B), the adjustment (src:436)
GIVEN `the household is in the affected area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(h)(3)(B) the Secretary must adjust the issuance methods and the reporting and other application requirements for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is in the affected area`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall adjust issuance methods and reporting and other application requirements to be consistent with what is practicable under actual conditions in the affected area"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the adjustment is to what is practicable "under actual conditions in the affected area"

§ `s 2014(i) Sponsored aliens`

-- src:452 | (E) The provisions of this subsection shall not apply with respect to any alien who is a member of the sponsor’s household or to any alien who is under 18 years of age.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(E), exceptions (src:452)
GIVEN `the alien is a member of the sponsor's household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alien is under 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(i)(2)(E) the subsection applies to the alien` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the alien is a member of the sponsor's household` OR `the alien is under 18 years of age`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this subsection shall not apply with respect to any alien who is a member of the sponsor's household or to any alien who is under 18 years of age"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception names two classes and does not say that the subsection applies to everyone else

-- src:438 | For purposes of determining eligibility for and the amount of benefits under this chapter for an individual who is an alien as described in section 2015(f)(2)(B) of this title, the income and resources of any person who as a sponsor of such individual’s entry into the United States executed an affidavit of support or similar agreement with respect to such individual, and the income and resources of the sponsor’s spouse if such spouse is living with the sponsor, shall be deemed to be the income and resources of such individual for a period of three years after the individual’s entry into the United States.
@ref s 2014(i)(1), first sentence (src:438)
GIVEN `s 2015(f)(2)(B) the individual is an alien as described in section 2015(f)(2)(B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a person executed an affidavit of support or similar agreement as a sponsor of the individual's entry into the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alien is a member of the sponsor's household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alien is under 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the individual's entry into the United States` IS A DATE
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(i)(1) the income and resources of the sponsor are deemed to be the income and resources of the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2014(i)(2)(E) the subsection applies to the alien` `the alien is a member of the sponsor's household` `the alien is under 18 years of age`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- the exception of paragraph (2)(E): "The provisions of this subsection shall not apply"
        IF NOT (`snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(f)(2)(B) the individual is an alien as described in section 2015(f)(2)(B)`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is for "an individual who is an alien as described in section 2015(f)(2)(B)"
        IF NOT `a person executed an affidavit of support or similar agreement as a sponsor of the individual's entry into the United States`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph deems the income of "any person who as a sponsor of such individual's entry into the United States executed an affidavit of support or similar agreement"
        IF `the date of the determination` AT LEAST `the date of the individual's entry into the United States` AND `snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date of the individual's entry into the United States` `the date of the determination` LESS THAN 36
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be deemed to be the income and resources of such individual for a period of three years after the individual's entry into the United States"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is "for a period of three years after the individual's entry into the United States" and the determination is outside it

-- src:438 | (1) For purposes of determining eligibility for and the amount of benefits under this chapter for an individual who is an alien as described in section 2015(f)(2)(B) of this title, the income and resources of any person who as a sponsor of such individual’s entry into the United States executed an affidavit of support or similar agreement with respect to such individual, and the income and resources of the sponsor’s spouse if such spouse is living with the sponsor, shall be deemed to be the income and resources of such individual for a period of three years after the individual’s entry into the United States. Any such income deemed to be income of such individual shall be treated as unearned income of such individual.
@ref s 2014(i)(1), second sentence (src:438)
GIVEN `the monthly amount of the income deemed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income item`
`s 2014(i)(1) the deemed income as an item of the individual's income` MEANS
    `Income item` WITH
        `description` IS "income deemed to be the individual's under section 2014(i)"
        `monthly amount in dollars` IS `the monthly amount of the income deemed, in dollars`
        `earned income` IS FALSE

-- src:440 | (A) The amount of income of a sponsor, and the sponsor’s spouse if living with the sponsor, which shall be deemed to be the unearned income of an alien for any year shall be determined as follows:
-- src:441 | (i) the total yearly rate of earned and unearned income of such sponsor, and such sponsor’s spouse if such spouse is living with the sponsor, shall be determined for such year under rules prescribed by the Secretary;
-- src:442 | (ii) the amount determined under clause (i) of this subparagraph shall be reduced by an amount equal to the income eligibility standard as determined under subsection (c) for a household equal in size to the sponsor, the sponsor’s spouse if living with the sponsor, and any persons dependent upon or receiving support from the sponsor or the sponsor’s spouse if the spouse is living with the sponsor; and
-- src:443 | (iii) the monthly income attributed to such alien shall be one-twelfth of the amount calculated under clause (ii) of this subparagraph.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(A), the income deemed (src:440-443)
GIVEN `the total yearly rate of earned and unearned income of the sponsor, and of the sponsor's spouse if living with the sponsor, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the income eligibility standard under subsection (c) for a household of the size in clause (ii), for a year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(i)(2)(A) the monthly income attributed to the alien` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the income eligibility standard under subsection (c) for a household of the size in clause (ii), for a year, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the total yearly rate of earned and unearned income of the sponsor, and of the sponsor's spouse if living with the sponsor, in dollars`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the amount after the reduction is below nothing, and the text does not say whether the income attributed is then nothing
        OTHERWISE JUST ((`the total yearly rate of earned and unearned income of the sponsor, and of the sponsor's spouse if living with the sponsor, in dollars` MINUS `the income eligibility standard under subsection (c) for a household of the size in clause (ii), for a year, in dollars`) DIVIDED BY 12)  -- "the monthly income attributed to such alien shall be one-twelfth of the amount calculated under clause (ii)"

-- src:442 | (ii) the amount determined under clause (i) of this subparagraph shall be reduced by an amount equal to the income eligibility standard as determined under subsection (c) for a household equal in size to the sponsor, the sponsor’s spouse if living with the sponsor, and any persons dependent upon or receiving support from the sponsor or the sponsor’s spouse if the spouse is living with the sponsor; and
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(A)(ii), the size of the household (src:442)
GIVEN `the sponsor's spouse is living with the sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons dependent upon or receiving support from the sponsor or the sponsor's spouse if the spouse is living with the sponsor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(i)(2)(A)(ii) the size of the sponsor's household` MEANS
    1 PLUS (IF `the sponsor's spouse is living with the sponsor` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS `the number of persons dependent upon or receiving support from the sponsor or the sponsor's spouse if the spouse is living with the sponsor`

-- src:444 | (B) The amount of resources of a sponsor, and the sponsor’s spouse if living with the sponsor, which shall be deemed to be the resources of an alien for any year shall be determined as follows:
-- src:445 | (i) the total amount of the resources of such sponsor and such sponsor’s spouse if such spouse is living with the sponsor shall be determined under rules prescribed by the Secretary;
-- src:446 | (ii) the amount determined under clause (i) of this subparagraph shall be reduced by $1,500; and
-- src:447 | (iii) the resources determined under clause (ii) of this subparagraph shall be deemed to be resources of such alien in addition to any resources of such alien.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(B), the resources deemed (src:444-447)
GIVEN `the total amount of the resources of the sponsor and of the sponsor's spouse if living with the sponsor, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(i)(2)(B) the resources deemed to be the alien's resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the total amount of the resources of the sponsor and of the sponsor's spouse if living with the sponsor, in dollars` LESS THAN 1500
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the amount after the reduction of $1,500 is below nothing, and the text does not say whether the resources deemed are then nothing
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the total amount of the resources of the sponsor and of the sponsor's spouse if living with the sponsor, in dollars` MINUS 1500)  -- "the amount determined under clause (i) of this subparagraph shall be reduced by $1,500"

-- src:447 | (iii) the resources determined under clause (ii) of this subparagraph shall be deemed to be resources of such alien in addition to any resources of such alien.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(B)(iii), in addition to the alien's own resources (src:447)
GIVEN `the resources of the alien, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the resources deemed under clause (ii), in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(i)(2)(B)(iii) the resources of the alien with the resources deemed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the resources deemed under clause (ii), in dollars`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount deemed under clause (ii) was not determined
        WHEN JUST deemed THEN JUST (`the resources of the alien, in dollars` PLUS deemed)

-- src:449 | Any individual who is an alien shall, during the period of three years after entry into the United States, in order to be an eligible individual or eligible spouse for purposes of this chapter, be required to provide to the State agency such information and documentation with respect to the alien’s sponsor and sponsor’s spouse as may be necessary in order for the State agency to make any determination required under this section, and to obtain any cooperation from such sponsor necessary for any such determination.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(C)(i), information and cooperation (src:449)
GIVEN `the alien has provided the State agency the information and documentation about the sponsor and the sponsor's spouse, and obtained the cooperation of the sponsor, that are necessary for the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the alien's entry into the United States` IS A DATE
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(i)(2)(C)(i) the alien is barred from being an eligible individual or eligible spouse for not providing the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date of the determination` AT LEAST `the date of the alien's entry into the United States` AND `snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date of the alien's entry into the United States` `the date of the determination` LESS THAN 36)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is "during the period of three years after entry into the United States"
        IF `the alien has provided the State agency the information and documentation about the sponsor and the sponsor's spouse, and obtained the cooperation of the sponsor, that are necessary for the determination`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the information is required only "in order to be an eligible individual or eligible spouse", so an alien who provides it is not barred by this clause (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "in order to be an eligible individual or eligible spouse for purposes of this chapter, be required to provide to the State agency such information and documentation"

-- src:449 | Such alien shall also be required to provide such information and documentation which such alien or the sponsor provided in support of such alien’s immigration application as the State agency may request.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(C)(i), the application information (src:449)
GIVEN `the information and documentation is what the alien or the sponsor provided in support of the alien's immigration application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has requested the information and documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(i)(2)(C)(i) the alien is required to provide the information and documentation given in support of the immigration application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information and documentation is what the alien or the sponsor provided in support of the alien's immigration application` AND `the State agency has requested the information and documentation`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Such alien shall also be required to provide such information and documentation which such alien or the sponsor provided in support of such alien's immigration application as the State agency may request"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches the information "which such alien or the sponsor provided in support of such alien's immigration application" "as the State agency may request"; whether the first sentence's three-year period also limits it is not said, so no period is applied (fork F-I2)

-- src:451 | (D) Any sponsor of an alien, and such alien, shall be jointly and severably liable for an amount equal to any overpayment made to such alien during the period of three years after such alien’s entry into the United States, on account of such sponsor’s failure to provide correct information under the provisions of this section, except where such sponsor was without fault, or where good cause for such failure existed. Any such overpayment which is not repaid shall be recovered in accordance with the provisions of section 2022(b) of this title.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(D), liability for an overpayment (src:451)
GIVEN `the date of the alien's entry into the United States` IS A DATE
      `the date the overpayment was made to the alien` IS A DATE
      `the overpayment was made on account of the sponsor's failure to provide correct information under the provisions of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sponsor was without fault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `good cause for the failure existed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(i)(2)(D) the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable for the overpayment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the overpayment was made on account of the sponsor's failure to provide correct information under the provisions of this section` AND `the date the overpayment was made to the alien` AT LEAST `the date of the alien's entry into the United States` AND `snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date of the alien's entry into the United States` `the date the overpayment was made to the alien` LESS THAN 36)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the liability is for an overpayment made "during the period of three years after such alien's entry" and "on account of such sponsor's failure to provide correct information"
        IF `the sponsor was without fault` OR `good cause for the failure existed`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where such sponsor was without fault, or where good cause for such failure existed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Any sponsor of an alien, and such alien, shall be jointly and severably liable for an amount equal to any overpayment"

-- src:451 | (D) Any sponsor of an alien, and such alien, shall be jointly and severably liable for an amount equal to any overpayment made to such alien during the period of three years after such alien’s entry into the United States, on account of such sponsor’s failure to provide correct information under the provisions of this section, except where such sponsor was without fault, or where good cause for such failure existed. Any such overpayment which is not repaid shall be recovered in accordance with the provisions of section 2022(b) of this title.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(D), the amount (src:451)
GIVEN `the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(i)(2)(D) the amount for which the sponsor and the alien are each liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable`
            THEN JUST `the overpayment, in dollars`  -- jointly and severally: each is liable for the whole amount
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable`
            THEN JUST 0
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the liability exists was not determined

-- src:451 | (D) Any sponsor of an alien, and such alien, shall be jointly and severably liable for an amount equal to any overpayment made to such alien during the period of three years after such alien’s entry into the United States, on account of such sponsor’s failure to provide correct information under the provisions of this section, except where such sponsor was without fault, or where good cause for such failure existed. Any such overpayment which is not repaid shall be recovered in accordance with the provisions of section 2022(b) of this title.
@ref s 2014(i)(2)(D), recovery (src:451)
GIVEN `the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment has not been repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(i)(2)(D) the overpayment is to be recovered in accordance with section 2022(b)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable` AND `the overpayment has not been repaid`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Any such overpayment which is not repaid shall be recovered in accordance with the provisions of section 2022(b)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "any such overpayment which is not repaid"

§ `s 2014(j) Resource exemption for otherwise exempt households`

-- src:454 | Notwithstanding subsections (a) through (i), a State agency shall consider a household member who receives supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.], aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, II, X, XIV, or XVI of such Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq., 401 et seq., 1201 et seq., 1351 et seq., 1381 et seq.], or who receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) to have satisfied the resource limitations prescribed under subsection (g).
@ref s 2014(j) (src:454)
GIVEN member IS AN Individual
      `the member receives aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, II, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(j) the member is considered to have satisfied the resource limitations of subsection (g)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF member's `receives supplemental security income benefits` OR `the member receives aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, II, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act` OR `the member receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Act`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a State agency shall consider a household member who receives supplemental security income benefits ... to have satisfied the resource limitations prescribed under subsection (g)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for "a household member who receives" one of the three kinds of benefit

§ `s 2014(k) Assistance to third parties`

-- src:461 | (2) Paragraph (1) shall not apply to—
-- src:462 | (A) medical assistance;
-- src:463 | (B) child care assistance;
-- src:464 | (C) a payment or allowance described in subsection (d)(11);
-- src:465 | (D) assistance provided by a State or local housing authority;
-- src:466 | (E) emergency assistance for migrant or seasonal farmworker households during the period such households are in the job stream;
-- src:467 | (F) emergency and special assistance, to the extent excluded in regulations prescribed by the Secretary; or
-- src:468 | (G) assistance provided to a third party on behalf of a household under a State or local general assistance program, or another local basic assistance program comparable to general assistance (as determined by the Secretary), if, under State law, no assistance under the program may be provided directly to the household in the form of a cash payment.
@ref s 2014(k)(2), the exceptions (src:461-468)
GIVEN `the assistance is medical assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is child care assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is a payment or allowance described in subsection (d)(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided by a State or local housing authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is emergency assistance for a migrant or seasonal farmworker household during the period the household is in the job stream` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is emergency and special assistance, to the extent excluded in regulations prescribed by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided to a third party on behalf of a household under a State or local general assistance program, or another local basic assistance program comparable to general assistance, and under State law no assistance under the program may be provided directly to the household in the form of a cash payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(k)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the assistance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the assistance is medical assistance` OR `the assistance is child care assistance` OR `the assistance is a payment or allowance described in subsection (d)(11)` OR `the assistance is provided by a State or local housing authority` OR `the assistance is emergency assistance for a migrant or seasonal farmworker household during the period the household is in the job stream` OR `the assistance is emergency and special assistance, to the extent excluded in regulations prescribed by the Secretary` OR `the assistance is provided to a third party on behalf of a household under a State or local general assistance program, or another local basic assistance program comparable to general assistance, and under State law no assistance under the program may be provided directly to the household in the form of a cash payment`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Paragraph (1) shall not apply to— (A) medical assistance; (B) child care assistance"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names seven classes of assistance and does not say what applies to others

-- src:456 | (1) For purposes of subsection (d)(1), except as provided in paragraph (2), assistance provided to a third party on behalf of a household by a State or local government shall be considered money payable directly to the household if the assistance is provided in lieu of—
-- src:457 | (A) a regular benefit payable to the household for living expenses under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.); or
-- src:458 | (B) a benefit payable to the household for housing expenses under—
-- src:459 | (i) a State or local general assistance program; or
-- src:460 | (ii) another basic assistance program comparable to general assistance (as determined by the Secretary).
@ref s 2014(k)(1), assistance to a third party (src:456-460)
GIVEN `the assistance is provided to a third party on behalf of a household by a State or local government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided in lieu of a regular benefit payable to the household for living expenses under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided in lieu of a benefit payable to the household for housing expenses under a State or local general assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided in lieu of a benefit payable to the household for housing expenses under another basic assistance program comparable to general assistance, as determined by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2014(k)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the assistance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(k)(1) the assistance to a third party is considered money payable directly to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the assistance is provided to a third party on behalf of a household by a State or local government`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is for "assistance provided to a third party on behalf of a household by a State or local government"
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2014(k)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the assistance`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) shall not apply to"
        IF NOT (`the assistance is provided in lieu of a regular benefit payable to the household for living expenses under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` OR `the assistance is provided in lieu of a benefit payable to the household for housing expenses under a State or local general assistance program` OR `the assistance is provided in lieu of a benefit payable to the household for housing expenses under another basic assistance program comparable to general assistance, as determined by the Secretary`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be considered money payable directly to the household if the assistance is provided in lieu of" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "except as provided in paragraph (2), assistance provided to a third party on behalf of a household by a State or local government shall be considered money payable directly to the household"

-- src:469 | (3) For purposes of subsection (d)(1), educational loans on which payment is deferred, grants, scholarships, fellowships, veterans’ educational benefits, and the like that are provided to a third party on behalf of a household for living expenses shall be treated as money payable directly to the household.
@ref s 2014(k)(3), educational assistance (src:469)
GIVEN `the assistance is an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit, or the like` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided to a third party on behalf of the household for living expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(k)(3) the educational assistance is treated as money payable directly to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the assistance is an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit, or the like` AND `the assistance is provided to a third party on behalf of the household for living expenses`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "that are provided to a third party on behalf of a household for living expenses shall be treated as money payable directly to the household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is for educational assistance "provided to a third party on behalf of a household for living expenses"

-- src:471 | (A) Energy assistance payments.—
-- src:472 | For purposes of subsection (d)(1), a payment made under a State law (other than a law referred to in paragraph (2)(G)) to provide energy assistance to a household without an elderly or disabled member shall be considered money payable directly to the household.
@ref s 2014(k)(4)(A), energy assistance payments (src:471-472)
GIVEN `the payment is made under a State law, other than a law referred to in paragraph (2)(G), to provide energy assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(k)(4)(A) the energy assistance payment is considered money payable directly to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment is made under a State law, other than a law referred to in paragraph (2)(G), to provide energy assistance` AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a payment made under a State law ... to provide energy assistance to a household without an elderly or disabled member shall be considered money payable directly to the household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subparagraph is for a payment "to provide energy assistance to a household without an elderly or disabled member"

