    BRANCH
        IF `the expense is paid on behalf of the household under a State law to provide energy assistance` AND `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "an expense paid on behalf of a household with an elderly or disabled member under a State law to provide energy assistance shall be considered an out-of-pocket expense incurred and paid by the household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subparagraph is for an expense "paid on behalf of a household with an elderly or disabled member"

§ `s 2014(l) Earnings in on-the-job training`

-- src:476 | Notwithstanding section 181(a)(2) of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act [29 U.S.C. 3241(a)(2)], earnings to individuals participating in on-the-job training under title I of such Act [29 U.S.C. 3111 et seq.] shall be considered earned income for purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, except for dependents less than 19 years of age.
@ref s 2014(l) (src:476)
GIVEN person IS AN Individual
      `the individual participates in on-the-job training under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(l) the earnings of the individual in on-the-job training are considered earned income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual participates in on-the-job training under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for "earnings to individuals participating in on-the-job training under title I of such Act"
        IF `the individual is a dependent` AND person's `age in years` LESS THAN 19
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for dependents less than 19 years of age"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "earnings to individuals participating in on-the-job training under title I of such Act shall be considered earned income for purposes of the supplemental nutrition assistance program"

§ `s 2014(m) Simplified calculation of income for the self-employed`

DECLARE `s 2014(m) estimate for a type` HAS
    `s 2014(m) the type of self-employment income`                      IS A STRING
    `s 2014(m) the estimated income excluded under subsection (d)(9), in dollars` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 2014(m) method` HAS
    `s 2014(m) the estimate for all types of self-employment income, if the method allows one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 2014(m) the estimates for particular types of self-employment income`                   IS A LIST OF `s 2014(m) estimate for a type`

-- src:479 | the Secretary shall establish a procedure by which a State may submit a method, designed to not increase Federal costs, for the approval of the Secretary, that the Secretary determines will produce a reasonable estimate of income excluded under subsection (d)(9) in lieu of calculating the actual cost of producing self-employment income.
@ref s 2014(m)(1), the method (src:479)
GIVEN `the State has submitted the method` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the method is designed to not increase Federal costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has approved the method` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the method will produce a reasonable estimate of income excluded under subsection (d)(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(m)(1) the method may be used in lieu of calculating the actual cost of producing self-employment income` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State has submitted the method` AND `the method is designed to not increase Federal costs` AND `the Secretary has approved the method` AND `the Secretary determines that the method will produce a reasonable estimate of income excluded under subsection (d)(9)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a method, designed to not increase Federal costs, for the approval of the Secretary, that the Secretary determines will produce a reasonable estimate of income excluded under subsection (d)(9) in lieu of calculating the actual cost of producing self-employment income"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the method is one "designed to not increase Federal costs" that the Secretary approves and determines "will produce a reasonable estimate"

-- src:481 | The method submitted by a State under paragraph (1) may allow a State to estimate income for all types of self-employment income or may be limited to 1 or more types of self-employment income.
-- src:482 | (3) Differences for different types of income
-- src:483 | The method submitted by a State under paragraph (1) may differ for different types of self-employment income.
@ref s 2014(m)(2) and (3), the estimate for a type (src:481-483)
GIVEN method IS A `s 2014(m) method`
      kind IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(m)(3) the estimate of the method for the type of self-employment income` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN e YIELD e's `s 2014(m) the type of self-employment income` EQUALS kind) (method's `s 2014(m) the estimates for particular types of self-employment income`)
        WHEN EMPTY THEN method's `s 2014(m) the estimate for all types of self-employment income, if the method allows one`  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the method "may allow a State to estimate income for all types of self-employment income or may be limited to 1 or more types"
        WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (e's `s 2014(m) the estimated income excluded under subsection (d)(9), in dollars`)  -- "The method submitted by a State under paragraph (1) may differ for different types of self-employment income"

§ `s 2014(n) Child support payments`

-- src:485 | Regardless of whether a State agency elects to provide a deduction under subsection (e)(4), the Secretary shall establish simplified procedures to allow State agencies, at the option of the State agencies, to determine the amount of any legally obligated child support payments made, including procedures to allow the State agency to rely on information from the agency responsible for implementing the program under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 651 et seq.) concerning payments made in prior months in lieu of obtaining current information from the households.
@ref s 2014(n), the option (src:485)
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to use the simplified procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information concerns child support payments made in prior months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(n) the State agency may rely on information from the child support agency in lieu of obtaining current information from the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has chosen to use the simplified procedure` AND `the information concerns child support payments made in prior months`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "at the option of the State agencies, to determine the amount of any legally obligated child support payments made, including procedures to allow the State agency to rely on information from the agency responsible for implementing the program under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act concerning payments made in prior months in lieu of obtaining current information from the households"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the procedure is "at the option of the State agencies" and for "payments made in prior months"
